{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/dov6wf","slide":2,"text":"3 minutes. First spend about 45 seconds on the four familiar products. Ask what each must remember: orders, posts, playlists, or trips. The logos illustrate application variety only; do not suggest that these products all run on MySQL. Then let MySQL supply the students' likely picture: a client sends SQL to a server containing many subsystems. Ask them to name anything else they associate with a database server. Preserve the provisional answer: database means complicated software that stores and manages data. Do not correct it yet.\n\n[Sources]\n- https://dev.mysql.com/doc/dev/mysql-server/latest/PAGE_PROTOCOL.html\n- https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/9.2/en/innodb-architecture.html\n- https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/dd/MySQL_logo.svg\n- https://github.com/FortAwesome/Font-Awesome/blob/6.x/svgs/brands/amazon.svg\n- https://github.com/FortAwesome/Font-Awesome/blob/6.x/svgs/brands/instagram.svg\n- https://github.com/FortAwesome/Font-Awesome/blob/6.x/svgs/brands/spotify.svg\n- https://github.com/FortAwesome/Font-Awesome/blob/6.x/svgs/brands/uber.svg\n- /Users/stargazermiao/workspace/join-processing-datalog/doc/notes/01-a-little-database-a-few-questions.md\n[/Sources]"}
