{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/imfz3x","slide":3,"text":"2.5 minutes. Read the command from left to right: a CLI opens app.db, passes SQL to SQLite, and reads the same kind of users table students expect from MySQL. Ask: where is the server? Then ask what they are calling the database: the file, the SQLite library, or the tables inside it. Hold all answers. The contrast should weaken the equation database equals server without yet supplying the definition.\n\n[Sources]\n- https://sqlite.org/quickstart.html\n- https://sqlite.org/about.html\n- https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SQLite370.svg\n- https://github.com/FortAwesome/Font-Awesome/tree/6.x/svgs/regular/file.svg\n- /Users/stargazermiao/workspace/join-processing-datalog/doc/notes/01-a-little-database-a-few-questions.md\n[/Sources]"}
