{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/w9jnmi","slide":4,"text":"3.5 minutes. Point to the outer braces first: conceptually, this is one map from keys to typed values, not three unrelated records. Let students read the entries before naming Redis. Ask whether a database must manage tables. Then ask why a Redis server is not merely a shared HashMap; accept persistence, concurrency, remote access, data operations, and similar suggestions verbally without listing them on the slide. Reveal only the distinction database is not DBMS. Do not define database yet. Transition exactly: We now know the database is not the same thing as its management software. To say what a database is, first ask what counts as data.\n\n[Sources]\n- https://redis.io/docs/latest/develop/data-types/\n- https://redis.io/docs/latest/develop/data-types/hashes/\n- https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Redis_logo.svg\n- /Users/stargazermiao/workspace/join-processing-datalog/doc/notes/01-a-little-database-a-few-questions.md\n[/Sources]"}
