{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/rifj0b","slide":5,"text":"3 minutes. Ask in sequence: Is roads.xlsx data? Is roads.parquet data even if the format is unfamiliar? If a running program holds the same two road values, did they stop being data? Clarify one precise point: roads is a variable name or binding; the array value bound to it can serve as data. The equal signs mean the examples can carry the same logical values, not that their bytes or representations are identical. Do not teach XLSX or Parquet internals here. Conclude verbally: values are data; files and memory are different representations or locations. Transition exactly: However data is represented, software must turn a question into work. Where inside a DBMS does that happen?\n\n[Sources]\n- https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Microsoft_Office_Excel_(2025%E2%80%93present).svg\n- https://www.microsoft.com/en-gb/microsoft-365\n- https://parquet.apache.org/\n- https://github.com/apache/parquet-format/tree/master/logo\n- /Users/stargazermiao/workspace/join-processing-datalog/doc/notes/01-a-little-database-a-few-questions.md\n[/Sources]"}
